PARMA-DERIVED CODE AND DATA — USE NOTICE

This repository contains source code and data derived from the PARMA/PARMA4
cosmic-ray model distributed by the Japan Atomic Energy Agency (JAEA). The
materials supplied in the original project archive do not include a standard
open-source license grant. Nothing in this notice creates rights beyond those
granted by the original copyright holders.

The supplied upstream notice permits non-commercial use subject to citation of
the following publications:

1. T. Sato, "Analytical model for estimating terrestrial cosmic ray fluxes
   nearly anytime and anywhere in the world: Extension of PARMA/EXPACS,"
   PLOS ONE 10(12), e0144679 (2015).
2. T. Sato, "Analytical model for estimating the zenith angle dependence of
   terrestrial cosmic ray fluxes," PLOS ONE 11(8), e0160390 (2016).

Commercial use requires prior agreement with JAEA. Users are responsible for
confirming the applicable terms with JAEA and the original copyright holders
before redistribution, commercial use, or incorporation into another product.

Corrections and wrapper code added in this repository remain subject to the
rights and restrictions governing the underlying PARMA-derived materials.
